course: dictionary
lesson: 541
title: The ATM: a cash machine
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An ATM is a machine where you take money out of your bank account. ATM stands for automated teller machine, and in the UK people often say cash machine or cashpoint. «A cash machine asks for a secret number called a PIN.» Your PIN is the number that proves the card is yours.
explain: «A cash machine, or ATM, gives out cash from your account; you put in your card, cover the keypad while you type your PIN, and the money comes off your balance.» Your balance is how much money you have in the bank. When you take cash out, the balance goes down.
explain: Keep your PIN secret. Cover the keypad with your hand when you type it, so nobody can see the numbers.
fact: An ATM is a machine where people take money out of their bank account using a card and a PIN.
fact: ATM stands for automated teller machine. In the UK it is also called a cash machine or cashpoint.
fact: A PIN is a secret number, so keep it to yourself.
fact: «A cash machine, or ATM, reads the card's chip, checks the PIN with the bank and counts out notes.»
fact: At an ATM you can also check how much money you have.
exercise: «A cash machine asks for a secret number called a PIN.» What is a PIN? | A type of coin | A prize for good work | *A secret number that proves the card is yours | A kind of bank loan
exercise: Ahmed says an ATM is a shop. What is an ATM really? | A card that holds coins | A bus that goes to the bank | *A machine where you take money out of your account | A shop that sells cash
exercise: In the UK, which other word means the same as ATM? | Wallet | *Cashpoint | Coin jar | Cashbox
test: «Cover the keypad while you type your PIN.» Why do you do this? | *To keep your PIN secret from other people | To stop the screen going dark | To make the keypad warmer | To make the buttons louder
test: «The money comes off your balance.» What does balance mean here? | A scale for weighing coins | To walk along a wall with your arms out | A kind of football score | *How much money you have in your bank account
exam: What does ATM stand for? | Auto Tea Maker | Automatic table mover | *Automated teller machine | Any Time Money
